WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:13.336
For any claim: source and date, rewrite it until it can fail, access and incentives, evidence type, measured versus extrapolated, base rates, replication, verdict with a confidence level.

3
00:00:13.616 --> 00:00:16.667
For forecasts: ask for probabilities and score them.

4
00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:22.685
For your own work: every model output is a claim, and every check should fail differently from what it checks.

5
00:00:22.965 --> 00:00:32.715
The project for this elective puts both halves to work: a model selection playbook backed by your own eval, and an evidence-weighted brief on one current public claim.
